{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"Main_Section": "1. The following AI practices shall be prohibited:", "Sub_Section": "**3.5. Out of scope**", "Letter_Section": "**3.5.2. Manipulative, deceptive and exploitative AI systems that are not likely to cause significant harm**", "source": "clean_eu_proh_ai_act.md"}, "page_content": "- An online music platform uses an emotion recognition system to infer users\u2019 emotions and automatically recommends them songs in line with their moods, while avoiding excessive exposure to depressive songs. Since users are just listening to music and are not otherwise harmed or led to depression and anxiety, the system is not reasonably likely to cause significant harm.  \n- AI-enabled manipulative and deceptive techniques used in security training and other learning simulations that mimic phishing attempts to educate users on cybersecurity threats. These systems may deploy purposefully manipulative techniques (e.g., exploiting cognitive biases) without users\u2019 awareness that distort the behaviour, but this is done temporarily for beneficial training and awareness raising purposes and without causing significant harms.", "type": "Document"}}